domain:ui#2 · os-lizheng · session_012MmDsRT6hvZsQH9dTzn4CA

## Serial hold · 2026-11-12T20:09Z · claim 6833269771 parked

Blocked-by: #32774

The dev measured the mechanism on `main` `2f80f289` in the os-dev-report 6834640509 on this card.
- The copilot already announces both its in-tab draft write and its 撤销: `ChatPane` calls `emitMetadataRefresh()`.
- Studio's ledger (`usePendingDrafts`) and the Data rail re-read on that pulse.
- The **one** load that ignores it is the Data pillar's open-object load. Its effect is keyed `name#publishNonce#objReloadNonce` and never on the pulse, so `objDraft`, `objDraftChanges` and `hasDraft` stay stale. Those three feed the field inspector, the Form canvas and the header's own reading.

That effect lives in `ui/packages/app-shell/src/views/studio-design/StudioDesignSurface.tsx`. `domain:ui#6` holds that file for #32774. As ordered, the dev stopped at the held file: no PR, and the branch is empty.

**Probe readings.** These were measured on probes and never committed.
- On `main`: the inspector stays open with no chip, no new field on the canvas and no help text, and draft reads stay at 1.
- With the hunk below applied to an untracked copy: chip, new field and help text all appear, and draft reads go to 2.
- The header-count half (card step 5) does **not** reproduce on `main` at unit level, because an undo pulse over an empty ledger clears the line. On staging it is NOT MEASURED: it could be an older console build or `_drafts` lag.

**Resume.**
- When #32774 lands, or earlier if `domain:ui#6` writes a carve-out for these DataPillar lines, the card is re-dispatched with this hunk.
- The re-dispatch extends the same hold to the two sibling loads with the same gap: the base-object extension load (`extLoadedRef` effect, same file) and `useFormViewDraft.ts`.
- It needs three pins: the inspector re-reads after a copilot write; the header count clears after undo; and a CONTROL that a pulse does not replace the buffer while it is dirty, or for another object. Plus an ablation.
- Rejected alternative: routing the pulse through `onRolledBack` or `useDraftSaveGuard`'s reload. Both drop the dirty hold and close the inspector, and both use a conflict callback as a refresh channel.
- #32592's open decision (focus refetch, push) is untouched: this hunk only connects the existing in-tab pulse.

Resume-from: none (the branch `claude/issue-32610-copilot-draft-reread` equals `main`; the hunk below is the work)

<details><summary>The proposed hunk (+24 −2, measured on a copy; the held file was never edited)</summary>

```diff
--- a/ui/packages/app-shell/src/views/studio-design/StudioDesignSurface.tsx
+++ b/ui/packages/app-shell/src/views/studio-design/StudioDesignSurface.tsx
@@ -5771,6 +5771,14 @@
   // conflict's "reload" re-runs the load below for the open object.
   const [objReloadNonce, setObjReloadNonce] = React.useState(0);
   const reloadObjDraft = React.useCallback(() => setObjReloadNonce((n) => n + 1), []);
+  // objectstack#32610 — the copilot shares this document (ADR-0057 P3c): a
+  // draft its tool writes, and the discard its 撤销 runs, are announced on the
+  // assistant bus (`ChatPane`), the pulse the rail above already re-reads on.
+  // The open object re-reads on it too, so its field properties, the Form
+  // canvas and the header's own reading follow the server's draft without a
+  // reload. Held while the buffer carries work not yet sent (an edit, a save
+  // in flight): the pulse is released once that work is saved, never over it.
+  const objRefreshNonce = useMetadataRefreshNonce(dirty || extDirty || saving !== false);
   const {
     save: saveObjDraft,
     recordRead: recordObjRead,
@@ -5969,15 +5977,20 @@
     // clobber the in-progress form-layout draft the designer is editing.
     // Keyed by object + publishNonce: a package publish (nonce++) re-reads the
     // fresh published baseline; otherwise we never clobber an in-progress draft.
-    const loadKey = `${current.name}#${publishNonce}#${objReloadNonce}`;
+    const baseKey = `${current.name}#${publishNonce}#${objReloadNonce}`;
+    const loadKey = `${baseKey}#${objRefreshNonce}`;
     if (loadedNameRef.current === loadKey) return;
+    // objectstack#32610 — a re-read of the same object on the pulse alone
+    // keeps what the author has open (the selected field, the canvas): only
+    // what it shows is replaced. Any other load starts the object afresh.
+    const refreshOnly = loadedNameRef.current?.startsWith(`${baseKey}#`) === true;
     loadedNameRef.current = loadKey;
     let cancelled = false;
     // objectui#11331 — whether this run's load has settled (see the cleanup).
     let settled = false;
     setLoading(true);
     setError(null);
-    setFieldSel(null);
+    if (!refreshOnly) setFieldSel(null);
     // objectstack#27485 — kept CEL verdicts judged the buffer this load replaces.
     setCelVerdicts({});
     setPanelCelVerdicts({});
@@ -6027,6 +6040,12 @@
           return;
         }
         setObjDraft(authored.body);
+        // objectstack#32610 — a field the re-read no longer has (a discard
+        // took it away) is not left selected.
+        if (refreshOnly) {
+          const kept = new Set(readFields(authored.body.fields).entries.map((e) => e.name));
+          setFieldSel((sel) => (sel?.kind === 'field' && !kept.has(String(sel.id)) ? null : sel));
+        }
         setServedOnly(
           servedOnlyFields((draftBody ?? baseline).fields, [
             authored.body.fields,
@@ -6074,7 +6093,7 @@
         loadedNameRef.current = null;
       }
     };
-  }, [client, current, packageId, publishNonce, objReloadNonce, recordObjRead]);
+  }, [client, current, packageId, publishNonce, objReloadNonce, objRefreshNonce, recordObjRead]);

   // objectstack#28575 — the pair's extension of the open base object: its
   // pending draft at the pair, else its published row there, else a new
